# github-op-integrated MCP server configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to `.config/github-op-integrated.conf` and replace placeholders
# with values for your local environment. Do not commit `.config/*.conf`.
#
# Store secrets in 1Password or another secret manager. Use secret references
# such as `op://<VAULT>/<ITEM>/<FIELD>` here, not raw token values.

# GitHub Personal Access Token for github-op-integrated MCP server.
# Use a fine-grained PAT whose repository access includes this repository.
# Required permissions: Pull requests (read & write), Issues (read & write).
# Do not grant Contents: write.
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=op://<VAULT>/<ITEM>/<FIELD>

# MCP tools enabled for github-op-integrated.
# The allowlist covers PR / issue / review comment collaboration and read-only
# access to GitHub Actions (workflows, runs, jobs, artifacts, job logs).
# actions_run_trigger is deliberately excluded: triggering, re-running,
# cancelling and deleting workflow runs stay on `gh` with user approval.
GITHUB_TOOLS=list_pull_requests,search_pull_requests,pull_request_read,create_pull_request,update_pull_request,issue_read,list_issues,search_issues,issue_write,add_issue_comment,add_reply_to_pull_request_comment,pull_request_review_write,add_comment_to_pending_review,actions_get,actions_list,get_job_logs

# Optional: enable read-only mode. Write tools are disabled even if listed above.
# GITHUB_READ_ONLY=1

# Optional: use broader toolsets instead of the explicit allowlist above.
# Prefer GITHUB_TOOLS unless a reviewed guideline change requires toolsets.
# GITHUB_TOOLSETS=default

# Optional: GitHub Enterprise host. Leave unset for github.com.
# GITHUB_HOST=github.example.com
